---
// Services page: the page title and description; an introduction with the main heading and a lead paragraph; and one numbered section for each of the four services (websites, web applications, custom online tools, and other web projects), with an anchor for direct links, its number and name (the anchor and name come from site.ts, which the home page also uses for its links to these sections), what the service is, and the typical problems it solves. The introduction, the numbered sections, and their lists use the shared styles in global.css (each section below a hairline rule, its number and name placed beside the rest when the viewport is at least 48rem wide); this file styles the "Typical problems" label.
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { services, servicesPage, siteName } from "../lib/site";

const description =
	"Solvaxon's services: websites, web applications, custom online tools and other web-based projects, each with what it is and the typical problems it solves.";
---

<BaseLayout
	title={`${servicesPage.name} - ${siteName}`}
	description={description}
>
	<div class="page-width page-intro">
		<h1>{servicesPage.name}</h1>
		<p class="lead">
			Solvaxon builds websites, web applications, custom online tools and other
			web-based projects for individuals and businesses. Each service below
			explains what the work is and the typical problems it solves.
		</p>
	</div>
	<section class="page-width numbered-section" id={services.websites.anchor}>
		<header>
			<p class="number">01</p>
			<h2>{services.websites.name}</h2>
		</header>
		<div class="details">
			<p>
				A website gives a person, a business or an idea a home on the web. It is
				where people find out what you do and what you offer, and how to get in
				touch.
			</p>
			<h3>Typical problems</h3>
			<ul>
				<li>
					There is no website yet, so people who look you up find nothing.
				</li>
				<li>
					The current website is out of date and no longer reflects what you do.
				</li>
				<li>
					Visitors cannot quickly find what they came for, such as what you
					offer or how to contact you.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>
	<section
		class="page-width numbered-section"
		id={services.webApplications.anchor}
	>
		<header>
			<p class="number">02</p>
			<h2>{services.webApplications.name}</h2>
		</header>
		<div class="details">
			<p>
				A web application is software that people use in a web browser to get
				work done, such as handling bookings, orders or records, without
				installing anything.
			</p>
			<h3>Typical problems</h3>
			<ul>
				<li>
					A process runs on spreadsheets, email and paperwork that are hard to
					keep in order.
				</li>
				<li>
					Several people need to work with the same information from different
					places.
				</li>
				<li>Ready-made software does not fit the way you work.</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>
	<section
		class="page-width numbered-section"
		id={services.customOnlineTools.anchor}
	>
		<header>
			<p class="number">03</p>
			<h2>{services.customOnlineTools.name}</h2>
		</header>
		<div class="details">
			<p>
				A custom online tool does one specific job in the browser, built around
				the way you work: for example a price calculator, a quote builder or a
				form that collects exactly the information you need.
			</p>
			<h3>Typical problems</h3>
			<ul>
				<li>A repetitive task takes time that a simple tool could save.</li>
				<li>
					The same questions come up again and again, and a tool could answer
					them straight away.
				</li>
				<li>No ready-made tool does exactly what you need.</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>
	<section
		class="page-width numbered-section"
		id={services.otherWebProjects.anchor}
	>
		<header>
			<p class="number">04</p>
			<h2>{services.otherWebProjects.name}</h2>
		</header>
		<div class="details">
			<p>
				Not every idea fits neatly into one of the categories above. This
				service covers other web-based projects, for example a prototype that
				tests an idea before it is fully built.
			</p>
			<h3>Typical problems</h3>
			<ul>
				<li>
					You want to try an idea with real users before committing to a full
					build.
				</li>
				<li>The project needs parts of more than one of the services above.</li>
				<li>
					The idea is new and does not match a familiar type of website or
					application.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	h3 {
		margin: 1.5rem 0 0.5rem;
		color: var(--color-muted);
		font-size: 0.8125rem;
		font-weight: 400;
		letter-spacing: 0.16em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}
</style>
